  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Need assessment in Punia and Shabunda territories for HIP 2015 application .</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Punia and Shabunda territories are respectively situated in Maniema and South Kivu provinces. These territories are now a stage clashes between various militias and FARDC, but also between the militias themselves for either the leadership or control of mining squares. This brought the local populations of these territories to live in a state of movement and regular return.
To respond to some emergency needs, CAFOD has initiated a need assessment among the populations of these two territories with its partners Caritas Kindu and BDD Kasongo to apply for the HIP 2015 funds.</narrative>
  </description>
